===Arithmetic Operators===

{|
! Opcode
! Varops Budget Cost
|-
|OP_ADD
|Greater of two operand lengths * 3
|-
|OP_1ADD
|MAX(1, operand length) * 3
|-
|OP_SUB
|Greater of two operand lengths * 2
|-
|OP_1SUB
|MAX(1, operand length) * 2
|-
|OP_2MUL
|Operand length * 3
|-
|OP_2DIV
|Operand length * 2
|-
|OP_MUL
|Length of A + length of B + (length of A + 7) / 8 * (length of B) * 4  (BEWARE OVERFLOW)
|-
|OP_DIV
|Length of A * 9 + length of B * 2 + (length of A)^2 / 4  (BEWARE OVERFLOW)
|-
|OP_MOD
|Length of A * 9 + length of B * 2 + (length of A)^2 / 4  (BEWARE OVERFLOW)
|}

====Rationale====

The worst case for OP_ADD is that an overflow at the end requires a reallocation.

OP_SUB doesn't have this additional cost since it fails on underflow.

OP_1ADD and OP_1SUB are the same cost as ADD/SUB with a minimal 1 operand.

OP_2MUL and OP_2DIV are simply shifts, but OP_2MUL may have an extra copy on overflow.

See Appendix A for the cost calculations for OP_MUL, OP_DIV and OP_MOD.

